DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
951::$$$message_0004_0000_0000$$$::Well.[lr]::
952::$$$message_0004_0000_0001$$$::I have some time, so I'll clean my room.[lr]::
953::$$$message_0004_0000_0002$$$::It shouldn't be much work. I don't actually own a lot.[lr]::
954::$$$message_0004_0000_0003$$$::"Still, though..."[lr]::
955::$$$message_0004_0000_0004$$$::Strangely, my things have piled up day by day.[lr]::
956::$$$message_0004_0000_0005$$$::It's like having a rabbit that gives birth to a litter every time you take your eyes off it.::
957::$$$message_0004_0001_0000$$$::"...Was it a rabbit or a mouse? Anyway..."[lr]::
958::$$$message_0004_0001_0001$$$::I know the cause.[lr]::
959::$$$message_0004_0001_0002$$$::I know it very well, and there's nothing I can do to stop it.::
960::$$$message_0004_0002_0000$$$::"Eh, I can at least vacuum the place."[lr]::
961::$$$message_0004_0002_0001$$$::But I already know that if I get out the vacuum cleaner, I'll want to vacuum the neighboring rooms and won't be content until I've covered the entire building.[lr]::
962::$$$message_0004_0002_0002$$$::...This is supposed to be relaxing. I need to be sure to draw the line and stop somewhere.::
963::$$$message_0004_0003_0000$$$::I push the vacuum cleaner around.[se storage=se502.wav][lr]::
964::$$$message_0004_0003_0001$$$::Ahh, I've found the cause of the increasing stuff, or rather, the hoarding.[lr]::
965::$$$message_0004_0003_0002$$$::Just as I was wondering what she brought today...::
966::$$$message_0004_0004_0000$$$::"Hey! Whatcha doing, Shirou?"[lr]::
967::$$$message_0004_0004_0001$$$::"Vacuuming."[lr]::
968::$$$message_0004_0004_0002$$$::"Got it, well I'll see you later[line len=2]"[lr]::
969::$$$message_0004_0004_0003$$$::"Hold it."[lr]::
970::$$$message_0004_0004_0004$$$::Don't just drop a box of junk in my room and then leave.::
971::$$$message_0004_0005_0000$$$::"What's that, Fuji-nee?"[lr]::
972::$$$message_0004_0005_0001$$$::"Huh? Oh, just something I thought you'd need for your winter hibernation."::
973::$$$message_0004_0006_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
974::$$$message_0004_0006_0001$$$::Ha ha. Do I look like I'm really that type?[lr]::
975::$$$message_0004_0006_0002$$$::Also, junk wouldn't help someone hibernate.::
976::$$$message_0004_0007_0000$$$::"...Fuji-nee. This is my bedroom, not a beaver's dam... Mm, maybe a crow's nest would be a better metaphor."::
977::$$$message_0004_0008_0000$$$::"It does look just like one, now that you mention it.[lr]::
978::$$$message_0004_0008_0001$$$::Crows these days are no joke, though. They're [font italic=true]wild[font italic=false] in every sense of the word, and they even build their nests out of laundry hangers."::
979::$$$message_0004_0009_0000$$$::Huh. They even use hangers in their nests? That reminds me of a puzzle game.[lr]::
980::$$$message_0004_0009_0001$$$::Crows are supposed to be smart, but they're adaptable too.[lr]::
981::$$$message_0004_0009_0002$$$::"Anyway, my point is..."::
982::$$$message_0004_0010_0000$$$::My bedroom is not a storage space.[lr]::
983::$$$message_0004_0010_0001$$$::The shed in the yard has already turned into one of Fuji-nee's storerooms. I won't let her take over this space, too. I wish she'd build a nest in her own house...::
984::$$$message_0004_0011_0000$$$::"...Mgh. Are you planning to hibernate in my room?"[lr]::
985::$$$message_0004_0011_0001$$$::"Huh? Do tigers hibernate?"[lr]::
986::$$$message_0004_0011_0002$$$::"Bears do, but tigers don't...I think."[lr]::
987::$$$message_0004_0011_0003$$$::Is she saying she'd hibernate if she found out that tigers do?[lr]::
988::$$$message_0004_0011_0004$$$::...Actually, I can imagine her trying to pull it off.::
989::$$$message_0004_0012_0000$$$::"Hibernating like an animal sounds nice. I wonder what it's like to spend the whooole winter sleeping in a cave."[lr]::
990::$$$message_0004_0012_0001$$$::"Well, you'd have to eat a lot in the fall, and you would be all skin and bones come spring."::
991::$$$message_0004_0013_0000$$$::"So you mean I'd get to scarf down as much as I can during fall when everything's ripe for the taking, and wake up in the spring with a successful diet!?"[lr]::
992::$$$message_0004_0013_0001$$$::Man, I sometimes wish she'd hand over some of whatever it is that keeps her so upbeat.::
993::$$$message_0004_0014_0000$$$::"Now I actually want to try it."[lr]::
994::$$$message_0004_0014_0001$$$::"...What about your job?"[lr]::
995::$$$message_0004_0014_0002$$$::"I can just take winter hibernation leave... That doesn't exist, huh."[lr]::
996::$$$message_0004_0014_0003$$$::Just use your paid time off during winter break.[lr]::
997::$$$message_0004_0014_0004$$$::And then bury yourself under the kotatsu. I hear it turns people into lazy bums.::
998::$$$message_0004_0015_0000$$$::"So, Fuji-nee... That looks like a box for persimmons, but what exactly are you keeping in there?"[lr]::
999::$$$message_0004_0015_0001$$$::"Huh? Persimmons, obviously."[lr]::
1000::$$$message_0004_0015_0002$$$::Well, I suppo[line len=2]Wait, no.[lr]::
1001::$$$message_0004_0015_0003$$$::Are they actually persimmons?::
1002::$$$message_0004_0016_0000$$$::"It was SUCH a pain to haul them over here!"[lr]::
1003::$$$message_0004_0016_0001$$$::"Thanks for doing that...but why are you putting them in my room?"[lr]::
1004::$$$message_0004_0016_0002$$$::"The kitchen's too cramped, so I was looking for a place to park 'em. But I also don't want to leave them where nobody's around. They'd get forgotten, right? So I decided your room was the best place for them."::
1005::$$$message_0004_0017_0000$$$::"...Haah. I see.[lr]::
1006::$$$message_0004_0017_0001$$$::But Fuji-nee, didn't you put a bunch of mandarins and watermelons in the living room before?"[lr]::
1007::$$$message_0004_0017_0002$$$::"I did... But now that Saber and Sakura are around, I feel bad making a mess of the living room."::
1008::$$$message_0004_0018_0000$$$::"How incredibly thoughtful of you. So what made you think it's okay to make a mess of my room?[lr]::
1009::$$$message_0004_0018_0001$$$::...Hah!"[lr]::
1010::$$$message_0004_0018_0002$$$::I use the vacuum cleaner as a tool to open the box.[lr]::
1011::$$$message_0004_0018_0003$$$::...Inside, I see rows of bright, glossy persimmons.::
1012::$$$message_0004_0019_0000$$$::"I figured you'd need some feed if you're going to hibernate."[lr]::
1013::$$$message_0004_0019_0001$$$::"I already said I don't hibernate... Is this another gift from the Fujimura Group?"[lr]::
1014::$$$message_0004_0019_0002$$$::"Yep. We've got a TON of them."::
1015::$$$message_0004_0020_0000$$$::They must have really gotten a big shipment in, then.[lr]::
1016::$$$message_0004_0020_0001$$$::For whatever reason, they get so much fruit every season that I wonder if they're bound for some farmer's market.[lr]::
1017::$$$message_0004_0020_0002$$$::Grandpa Raiga once said it was the price for being part of the family.::
1018::$$$message_0004_0021_0000$$$::"We had so many that I thought about drying them outside."[lr]::
1019::$$$message_0004_0021_0001$$$::"Dried persimmons are sour, you know. What kind of prank were they thinking, sending them to someone raw..."::
1020::$$$message_0004_0022_0000$$$::Anyway, we have two boxes of persimmons.[lr]::
1021::$$$message_0004_0022_0001$$$::I pick one up and find that it's rather ripe and plump.::
1022::$$$message_0004_0023_0000$$$::"We'd better eat this soon."[lr]::
1023::$$$message_0004_0023_0001$$$::"I know, right!?[lr]::
1024::$$$message_0004_0023_0002$$$::Might as well be a persimmon festival at my house. Persimmons for breakfast, lunch, and dinner! I wanted to share some of the fall spirit with you! That's how considerate I am."::
1025::$$$message_0004_0024_0000$$$::Considerate. Rather than dumping what you can't finish on me. Uh huh.[lr]::
1026::$$$message_0004_0024_0001$$$::Still, they aren't bad as far as persimmons go. Actually, these are great quality.::
1027::$$$message_0004_0025_0000$$$::"It would be a waste if these spoiled."[lr]::
1028::$$$message_0004_0025_0001$$$::"I think it'll be okay. They'll be gone soon if everyone eats some."[lr]::
1029::$$$message_0004_0025_0002$$$::"We had just enough people for the mandarins, but persimmons, huh... The peaches and pears went quickly enough, true."::
1030::$$$message_0004_0026_0000$$$::I recall the assortment of fruits that have gone through our house.[lr]::
1031::$$$message_0004_0026_0001$$$::We have a lot more people to consume them than half a year ago, so they should go quickly.::
1032::$$$message_0004_0027_0000$$$::"I've still got mandarins and apples waiting to be brought over... I think Saber can eat a lot of them."[lr]::
1033::$$$message_0004_0027_0001$$$::"...At least we can use persimmons and apples in cooking. Anyway, I'm putting these somewhere else."::
1034::$$$message_0004_0028_0000$$$::I can't clean my room with these in the way.[lr]::
1035::$$$message_0004_0028_0001$$$::The room on the north side is open, so I can just set it down in the hall around there.::
1036::$$$message_0004_0029_0000$$$::"You should at least keep one box for your hiber..."[lr]::
1037::$$$message_0004_0029_0001$$$::"I really don't need that many! Come on, help."[lr]::
1038::$$$message_0004_0029_0002$$$::"Okay, okay. [wvl][shock vmax=20 time=800 count=3]Hup!"::
900993::$$$message_9004_0014_0000$$$::"Now I actually want to try it."[r]::

